Test remote session recovery with current Codex

Pin the isolated test package to Codex 0.154.0 so integration tests
cover the CLI used in practical sessions without replacing the
externally provided interactive Codex.

Wait for the fresh-thread welcome screen before submitting test prompts.
The startup draft composer accepts edits while discarding Enter, so an
early submission otherwise stalls before exercising the remote session.

The existing codex_relaunch_resumes_last_remote_session test now
reproduces "Permission overrides are not supported when resuming a
remote task." It passed with 0.147.0. Rumpel still passes its default
permission bypass flag on resume, so this regression remains failing
pending a fix.

Validation: all four required smoke tests passed. On 0.154.0 the Codex
filter passes 18 tests and fails only the resume reproducer, including
its retry. The host-network test also passed in isolation.
